        ecrm:P126_employed      "Woven silk.\nGround of light blue taffeta weave using one warp and one weft thread. The ribbon with three supplementary, brocading silk threads in red, mustard and ivory. The roses made of a red melange thread (i.e. the one red thread consisting of three coloured thread). One part of the brocading is bound in a twill on the back kept in place by the warp thread."@en ;
